ally-nationally-and-globally-significant-causing-and-contributing-to-plaintiffs-climate-injuries)1218 0 R(conclusion)1238 0 R(d-neither-the-mepa-limitation-nor-the-judicial-prohibition-survive-strict-scrutiny)1231 0 R(i-declaratory-relief-alone-establishes-redressability-for-plaintiffs-injuries)1221 0 R(i-defendants-concede-plaintiffs-are-experiencing-justiciable-injuries-caused-by-ghg-pollution-and-climate-change)1211 0 R(i-plaintiffs-have-proven-case-or-controversy-standing)1209 0 R(i-plaintiffs-mental-health-is-not-genuinely-in-controversy)1236 0 R(i-the-mepa-limitation-and-defendants-resulting-uninformed-and-unfettered-permitting-decisions-cause-plaintiffs-injuries)1214 0 R(ii-declaring-the-mepa-limitation-and-judicial-prohibition-unconstitutional-and-enjoining-their-implementation-will-alleviate-plaintiffs-climate-injuries)1223 0 R(ii-defendants-failed-to-establish-good-cause-for-rule-35-examinations)1237 0 R(ii-plaintiffs-also-have-standing-to-prevent-further-infringement-of-their-constitutional-rights)1212 0 R(ii-the-district-court-correctly-applied-montanas-constitutional-jurisprudence-to-conclude-the-mepa-limitation-and-judicial-prohibition-are-unconstitutional)1227 0 R(ii-the-mepa-limitation-causes-and-contributes-to-plaintiffs-climate-injuries)1215 0 R(iii-the-2023-mepa-limitation-would-have-continued-to-cause-and-exacerbate-plaintiffs-injuries)1219 0 R(iii-the-district-court-correctly-concluded-that-the-judicial-prohibition-is-not-a-barrier-to-redressability)1226 0 R(iii-the-district-courts-denial-of-defendants-request-for-rule-35-examinations-was-not-an-abuse-of-discretion)1232 0 R(standards-of-review)1206 0 R(statement-of-facts-and-procedural-history)1203 0 R(statement-of-the-case)1202 0 R(statement-of-the-issues-presented-for-review)1201 0 R(summary-of-the-argument)1207 0 R]>>>>>>
